// The United States Court of Federal Claims (lit/cofc), ported from
// packs/cofc-court-of-federal-claims.json. Section modules 01-06 hold the
// procedure graph in pack node order; the rules-* modules hold its
// deadlines, each counted by lit/core's RCFC 6 and tested inline. Cites to
// RCFC Appendices A, C, H and J and to case law stay holes carrying the
// legacy text: those sources are not vendored under sources/.
module cofc

group threshold-group: "Threshold: Accrual, Limitations, §1500"
group bid-protest-group: "Bid Protest Branch (28 U.S.C. §1491(b), Appendix C)"
group pleading-group: "Complaint, Service & Rule 12"
group general-track-group: "General Civil Track (RCFC 16, 26-37, 56)"
group adr-group: "ADR Off-Ramp (Appendix H)"
group patent-track-group: "§1498 Patent Track (Appendix J)"
group trial-post-trial-group: "Trial & Post-Trial (RCFC 52, 58, 59, 54, EAJA)"

/// An option the matter no longer has (SPEC §5.6): the claim's own
/// character forecloses it, or a party gave it up. `option` names the edge
/// (`e-filingfork-protest`), the event cites the authority that forecloses
/// it, and replay removes the edge for the rest of the matter without
/// moving it. A matter-level fact, not procedure, so no edge takes it.
event Forfeited(option: String)
